  "ts": "2026-05-26T08:31:54.20652Z",
  "content": "Event log filenames use nanosecond timestamps: 20060102T150405.000000000Z-\u003c8charID\u003e.json. An earlier bug used millisecond precision - two related events (an update + its companion embedding) routinely landed in the same millisecond, leaving the UUID suffix to tiebreak lexically at random. That broke reconcile's \"embedding is valid only if its filename \u003e last content-change filename\" rule. The integration test in cmd/internal/server/reconcile_test.go (TestSyncRoundTrip) caught this. Don't downgrade the precision.",
  "tags": [
    "gotcha",
    "events",
    "memlog",
    "reconcile"
  ],
